# Ignore rules for the SOURCE tree (tree/) — NOT for the lab, and NOT a .gitignore.
#
# tools/bootstrap.sh installs this into tree/ two ways: as a generated,
# self-ignoring tree/.gitignore (so editors, ripgrep and friends honour it
# natively), and as tree's core.excludesFile (a backstop, because `git clean
# -xdf` deletes the generated file — it is itself ignored). See
# docs/reorg-plan.md.
#
# Why it lives here: `upstream` and every feature branch commit NO .gitignore at
# all, so `git diff upstream feature/X` is exactly the mailable patch with no
# infra noise. Never commit a .gitignore into tree/.
#
# Build artefacts and locally-generated runtime files only. Source that upstream
# ships (including the hand-written Makefiles under riscos-progs/) is
# deliberately NOT ignored.

# --- Qt5 / qmake build artefacts (generated in src/qt5/) ---
/src/qt5/Makefile
/src/qt5/Makefile.Debug
/src/qt5/Makefile.Release
/src/qt5/.qmake.stash
/src/qt5/object_script.*
/src/qt5/release/
/src/qt5/debug/

# Compiled objects and qmake-generated sources (moc_*, qrc_*, ui_*)
*.o
moc_*.cpp
qrc_*.cpp
ui_*.h

# --- Built emulator binaries (qmake writes these to the source-tree root) ---
/rpcemu-interpreter*
/rpcemu-recompiler*
/RPCEmu-Interpreter*
/RPCEmu-Recompiler*

# --- Runtime-generated files ---
rpclog.txt

# --- Local ROM and hard-disc images (large / copyrighted — never commit) ---
/roms/*.rom
*.hdf

# cmos.ram and rpc.cfg are TRACKED by upstream, so they CANNOT be ignored here —
# .gitignore has no effect on a tracked file. `base` used to delete them; a
# branch off `upstream` does not. They are only dirtied by running the emulator
# from the source-tree root, so don't: `make run` launches an install, whose
# datadir is the install directory. See docs/reorg-plan.md.

# Not here, deliberately, because they are the lab's and are covered by the lab's
# own .gitignore: /installs/, /.devenv/, /.direnv/, devenv.local.*
